      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.882,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From Activity 12.2, we can explain that the population is a group of the same type of organisms in a habitat at a given time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.123,
            0.883,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can a habitat have only one type of living organism? What might happen then? If all organisms are the same, they would have the same requirements — food, water, space — leading to competition and possible scarcity of resources. What else do you think could happen?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.197,
            0.883,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Activities 12.1 and 12.2, you observed that different group of organisms live together in a habitat. A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "community",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " comprises different populations sharing the same habitat. The biotic components of a habitat, such as the plants, animals, and microorganisms together form the community. These organisms interact and depend on one another for survival."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.263,
            0.317,
            0.471,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ever heard of ..."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.353,
            0.865,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have seen brightly coloured flowers blooming around you. Have you ever looked closely at their parts? A flower has a stalk, green leafy structures called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sepals",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", coloured "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "petals",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and two reproductive"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.455,
            0.247,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
